  "boundaries": {
    "public": "MemoryQueryContext/MemoryContext use explicit owner-bound stores and named closed request/load callbacks. No Agent pointer, arbitrary business-state map, RawMessage or domain any. Runtime binds its existing side-model/event paths under existing ownership.",
    "selection": "Source defaults and zero/negative slicing; booleans, duplicate order and whole JSON syntax profile retained. Valid selection sliced to empty never invokes lexical fallback. Initial-list and fallback faults escape; ordinary query error/panic falls back.",
    "preparation": "Explicit enabled selection only; a typed load sender runs before prefix return. No live transcript mutation/capture or implicit provider/store acquisition.",
    "consolidation": "Explicit caller store/threshold independent of auto-tools. Initial listing outside best effort; origins preserve raw identity, replacement has partial effects/no rollback. No added lifecycle acquisition; runtime keeps its outer lifecycle.",
    "budget": "Source 200000-byte/2000-character defaults, negative preview slicing, stable character sort and UTF-8 byte accounting. Masked disk writes and raw previews retained. Later write failure retains files but original caller/result transcript; no unrelated compaction stage/model.",
